        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ab76384e-31bf-5583-92bb-dc2784e606e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Tarawa, Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, Battle of Saipan\n- Military units: Eighth Army Ranger Company\n- People: Rathvon M. Tompkins\n- Wars: World War II, Korean War\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought in the Pacific Theater of World War II from 20 to 23 November 1943.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was a decisive battle in the Korean War that took place from 25 November to 2 December 1950 along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in northwestern North Korea.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was also known as the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on and the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector.\n- The Eighth Army Ranger Company was best known for defending Hill 205 against a major Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River.\n- During the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, 41 of the 51 Rangers in the Eighth Army Ranger Company became casualties.\n- Rathvon M. Tompkins received the Silver Star for his actions during the Battle of Tarawa.\n- Rathvon M. Tompkins received the Navy Cross for his actions during the Battle of Saipan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a2dc2f34-81b3-5857-86bf-4df9b24254d0",
        "text": "Page: Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River. Sentence: The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, also known as the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on () or the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector (), was a decisive battle in the Korean War, and it took place from November 25 to December 2, 1950, along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in the northwestern part of North Korea.\nPage: Battle of Tarawa. Sentence: The Battle of Tarawa was a battle in the Pacific Theater of World War II that was fought on 20–23 November 1943.\nPage: Eighth Army Ranger Company. Sentence: It was best known for its defense of Hill 205 against an overwhelming Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River which resulted 41 of the 51 Rangers becoming casualties.\nPage: Rathvon M. Tompkins. Sentence: Richard KeHe was awarded the Navy Cross for his actions during the Battle of Saipan and the Silver Star for actions during the Battle of Tarawa.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
